%% Lifecycle of a single file on a cloud-tiering server endpoint - states, attributes and what moves it - Contoso profile
%% Source: Microsoft Learn Understand Azure File Sync cloud tiering and How to manage Azure File Sync tiered files (read 2026-09-03); docs/RULES.md TIER-02, TIER-03, SRV-09
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> NewLocal
    state "New on the server - not yet uploaded" as NewLocal
    state "Locally cached - size on disk equals logical size - attributes A only" as Cached
    state "Tiered - reparse point tag 0x8000001e - size on disk zero - attributes A L O and M on WS2019 plus" as Tiered
    state "Partially recalled - sparse - only the read range is on disk" as Partial
    state "Never tiered - below 2x cluster size with an 8 KiB floor, or matched by GhostingExclusionList" as Excluded

    NewLocal --> Cached : initial upload of the whole endpoint completes - the volume free space policy does not act before that
    NewLocal --> Tiered : low disk space mode only - tiering starts per file as soon as that file is uploaded
    Cached --> Excluded : file smaller than the minimum tierable size or listed in GhostingExclusionList
    Cached --> Tiered : hourly policy check tiers the coldest files off the heat map until the volume free space target is met
    Cached --> Tiered : date policy - not read or written for tierFilesOlderThanDays - only if free space already satisfies the volume policy
    Cached --> Tiered : Invoke-StorageSyncCloudTiering forces one file or one directory
    Tiered --> Partial : streaming read by a media player or a zip utility recalls only the requested range
    Partial --> Cached : the full read completes - the reparse point and the O attribute are removed
    Tiered --> Cached : a user opens the file and StorageSync.sys recalls it
    Tiered --> Cached : Invoke-StorageSyncFileRecall - up to 32 threads - Order CloudTieringPolicy stops at the policy limit
    Tiered --> Cached : proactive recall pulls down a change another endpoint made
    Tiered --> Tiered : recall while in low disk space mode is NOT persisted to disk - the next read recalls it again
    Excluded --> Cached : exclusions never apply to already tiered files - recall them explicitly

    note right of Tiered
      Heat position is MAX of last access, last modified, creation time.
      Azure File Sync tracks last access itself - do not turn on the NTFS
      last access time feature.
      Get-StorageSyncHeatStoreInformation shows the exact tiering and
      recall order with IndexName FilesToBeTieredBySpacePolicy,
      FilesToBeTieredByDatePolicy and OrderTieredFilesWillBeRecalled.
    end note

    note left of Cached
      Low disk space mode: entered when free space falls below
      MIN of 10 percent of the volume, the free-space policy in GiB, and 20 GiB.
      The agent then checks for files to tier every minute instead of every hour
      and stops persisting recalls. Telemetry event 19000 every minute,
      IsLowDiskMode true. Rule TIER-03.
    end note
